 #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1pn[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Task-bead backlog epic 2: agent isolation, poisoned slots, close [/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]         [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]guards, and toolchain drift[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]The five next-costliest open task beads (sase-163, sase-1p9, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase-o7, sase-1cs, sase-vr) are fixed on master and closed. The [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]land agent then proposes the next five-bead backlog epic under the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]same rules.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]4[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]1[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] wave[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]task_backlog_epic_2.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/task_backlog_epic_2.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim] Parent: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/task_backlog_epic_1.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1pn[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1pn/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Refuse cross-session messages into SASE Claude agents [/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-163)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]claude-isolation[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]claude-isolation: make ClaudeCodeProvider launches refuse cross-session [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]inbound messages and apply the claude_tools decision to the vendor async[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tools, with a provider-args regression test.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop a preservation refusal from poisoning its workspace slot [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1p9)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]slot-refusal[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]slot-refusal: remember launch-time nested-preservation refusals per [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]workspace, apply the slot_refusal decision, and raise one actionable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notification instead of failing every later launch there.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the epic close guard see upstream --epic-symbol rows [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-o7)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]close-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]close-guard: have sase bead close and sase bead epic-symbols read the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fetched default branch's Justfile as well as the local one, so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sibling-phase whitelist rows cannot escape the close.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the dev toolchain deterministic across CI and workspaces [bold black on #FFD75F][/bold #D7AFFF] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF](sase-1cs, sase-vr)[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]dev-toolchain[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]dev-toolchain: apply the toolchain_source decision so Textual, ruff and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mypy resolve to one declared version everywhere, refresh uv.lock, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fix any lint findings the chosen versions report.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-1pn","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-1pn.1","reasoning_effort":"high","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-4c77b76aaedea07c9499969550f0a657","started_at":"2026-10-29T14:48:00.165558+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"